# cycle/requests.jsonl — the FLEET & EQUIPMENT record's inbound door. Append-only.
#
# ⭐ THIS IS TRACK B's DOOR, NOT THE MOM-CYCLE'S. Read BACKLOG.md's opening:
# Fernwood carries TWO PRODUCTS in one repo — Track A, Mom's field journal, and
# Track B, Paul's fleet & equipment tracker. Different users, tone, cadence and
# definition of done. The mom-cycle (MOM-CYCLE-MAP.md) is Track A's loop and has
# NO BEAT for a vehicle record. Track B has no loop at all.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. On 2026-08-28 two vehicle facts surfaced from a comms sweep —
# two LMC Truck orders addressed to the house instead of the gatehouse, and a
# Golf GTI service visit with no serviceHistory entry. `ask-cycle.py` REFUSED
# both, correctly: Fernwood's only declared loop is the mom-cycle and neither ask
# belonged in it. They reached BACKLOG.md because a session remembered to put
# them there. This door is so the next one does not depend on remembering.
# `demand.py` had both logged as DEMONSTRATED DEMAND — 2 asks, no door.
#
# WHAT BELONGS HERE. A fact about a vehicle, a part, a piece of equipment, a
# service event or a delivery address that the Fernwood record has wrong, missing
# or unverified. ⚠️ The parts record is known wrong in BOTH directions
# ([[reference_parts_record_under_reports]]): it has under-reported what Paul
# OWNS and over-reported what he ORDERED. Absence is not evidence, and neither is
# a stated order — clear an order with an ORDER NUMBER.
#
#   python3 ~/.claude/tools/ask-cycle.py fernwood-fleet "<the fact + its evidence>" --from <project>
#
# WHAT DOES NOT BELONG HERE. Anything about Mom, her feedback, the journal, the
# viewer, or her asks — that is Track A and it rides the mom-cycle. Filing it
# here puts it where no beat reads it.
#
# ⚠️ NOTHING SWEEPS THIS FILE ON A CADENCE. Track B has no loop, so an entry is
# read when fleet work is next opened. A durable inbox, not an alarm; a
# time-sensitive fact also belongs on BACKLOG.md, which stays the canonical
# surface for Fernwood open work.
#
# Shape (one JSON object per line):
#   {"from":"security","what":"LMC order W7610655 shipped to the house, belonged at the gatehouse","opened":"2026-08-28"}
{"from": "photo-organizer", "what": "GTI 2026-07-21 — TEN photographs of repairs Paul says he did himself, Paul-ruled by voice 2026-08-28 as observed:gti-2016:repair:2026-07-21 (photo-organizer sweep 120, reports/project-review-never-reviewed-bursts.answers.json). His words: '76 through 85 [a]re repairs that I did on the GTI'. This repo's own inbound-door commit records that ask-cycle refused 'the GTI service visit with no serviceHistory entry' on 8/28 — this is dated photographic evidence for that gap. ⚠️ It evidences that work happened on that date and nothing more: WHAT was repaired is unread, and the VLM captions must not be used to say.", "opened": "2026-08-28", "status": "resolved", "closed": "2026-09-01", "disposition": "ALREADY IN THE RECORD — verified at fleet lap 1 beat 3. The 2026-07-21 GTI work is `sr-2026-07-21-cone-strike-repair-a` (DIY (Paul)): a traffic cone came off a truck ahead and was sucked under the car, damaging the grill and underbody panels, repaired in place with washers, zip ties and tape. It is not a thin row — it also carries a linked open item (\"Underbody + radiator/condenser eyeball (post cone-strike)\") and a downstream 2026-08-26 corroboration, where VW of Marietta quoted both front bumper vents and the card reasons that this is the cone strike showing through the in-place repair. So the ten photographs are CORROBORATING EVIDENCE for an existing row, not a missing event. ⭐ The ask was premised on 'a GTI service visit with no serviceHistory entry' — that refusal was about a SHOP VISIT; this date is DIY work and was recorded all along. Nothing was missing. WHAT REMAINS AVAILABLE, and it is optional: link the ten photographs as `photoEvidence` on that row. ⚠️ Note `photoEvidence` is one of the fields digest_vehicles DROPS, so linking them would not make them reachable by the assistant — see PRODUCT-ENGINE.md § the detail-vs-card split."}
{"from": "photo-organizer", "what": "A HANDWRITTEN BRONCO PARTS/SERVICE LIST EXISTS AS A PHOTOGRAPH, dated 2026-07-20, and NOBODY HAS READ IT. Two cards, Paul-ruled reference:bronco-1989:service-notes (photo-organizer sweep 120). His words: '74 and 75 [a]re pictures of documents for bronco records'. ⚠️ Deliberately NOT transcribed on the photo side: a value read off a photographed document is a model read, and the parts record is the one place this portfolio has measured being wrong in BOTH directions. The model's own caption mentions an 'Eddie Bauer badge' and 'rear window moulding' — quoted here ONLY to show the document is about Bronco trim, NOT as parts facts. What this ask is: an artifact pointer. Somebody with the parts register open should read the two photographs and reconcile; absence stays not-evidence and a stated order still clears only with an ORDER NUMBER.", "opened": "2026-08-28", "status": "routed", "routed_to": "BACKLOG.md Track B", "closed": "2026-09-01", "disposition": "ROUTED, NOT RESOLVED — fleet lap 1 beat 3. This one is real and stays open: two photographs of a handwritten Bronco parts/service document, dated 2026-07-20, and nothing has read them. ⛔ DELIBERATELY NOT read by this lap and not by an agent. A value read off a photographed handwritten document is a MODEL READ, and the parts record is the single place this portfolio has MEASURED being wrong in BOTH directions ([[reference_parts_record_under_reports]]): it has under-reported what Paul owns and over-reported what he ordered. The 2026-08-28 case study (a stated order and a stated cancellation, both false in one afternoon) is the same axis. So this needs the eyeball/verify path with Paul in it, not a transcription. Filed as open work in BACKLOG.md Track B with the tooling named. Absence stays not-evidence, and a stated order still clears only with an ORDER NUMBER."}

