{"from": "photo-organizer", "what": "BOLORES — SIX MONTHS OF RESTORATION, FROM THE PHOTOGRAPHS, IN PAUL'S OWN WORDS. photo-organizer lap 27 walked the whole vehicle-bolores album with him: 550 cards across three sheets, 316 rulings, 2025-09-26 → 2026-03-13. ⭐ READ THE NARRATIVE, NOT THIS ROW: photo-organizer/reports/bolores-restoration-narrative.md — 97 episodes, DERIVED by tools/bolores_narrative.py from the answers files (sweeps 144/145/146), every quote his verbatim sentence stored as a `paul_said` FIELD (not left inside prose). It exists because Paul asked for it: 'it may help kind of confirm the history of everything I've done to Dolores in that more detailed record I'm writing, so I don't wanna lose that granularity.' ⭐⭐ THE HEADLINE FINDINGS. (1) A COMPLETE REPAIR ARC NOBODY HAD: October 2025 'the tailgate latch rod that fell off inside' → the parts (sr-2025-10-24-rear-window-lift-motor, sr-2025-11-02-tailgate-latch-assembly, sr-2025-11-03-tailgate-latch-handle-rod) → November 'disassembling the tailgate and replacing a lot of components, including the motor and the latch mechanism' → 'the FIRST TIME that the rear tailgate window really worked from the dashboard switch.' Cause, parts, work and proof, dated and in order. THE FAILURE PREDATES THE PARTS BY A MONTH, which no receipt could show. (2) ⭐ A PART WAS REPLACED AND THE FAULT SURVIVED IT: 'me trying to replace the front driver side door lock actuator, and seeing that it STILL DIDN'T WORK.' Four months later he is still on it — 'trying to figure out the door lock actuator voltage thing.' A parts ledger records the purchase and can never record that it did not fix anything. (3) THREE OPEN ITEMS IN HIS OWN WORDS are listed in the narrative's own section, including card 199, 'where the dash had BROKEN SCREW HOLES — what I need to do to fix that', stated in the future tense. (4) OUTCOMES, not just work: the striker bushings on both front doors and the tailgate 'GREATLY REDUCED DOOR RATTLE'; a cigarette lighter